<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saito Dosan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1494–1556</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Saitō Dōsan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saito Dosan was a Japanese warlord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> who seized control of Mino province from the Toki family, earning the nickname 'viper of Mino'. Later legend made him a former oil merchant, though modern historians think his father began the family's rise. He married his daughter to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>, and was killed in 1556 fighting his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saito-yoshitatsu">Saito Yoshitatsu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saito-dosan.jpg" alt="Saito Dosan" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gameposo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saito_Dosan1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
